# The image bakes the pipeline source (see Dockerfile). Keep build junk out of
# it — these are either regenerated inside the container or local-only.
#
# NOTE: .dockerignore is NOT .gitignore. Patterns are matched with Go's
# filepath.Match against the path relative to the context root, so a bare
# `__pycache__/` matches ONLY a top-level directory of that name. Every pattern
# that should apply at any depth needs the `**/` prefix — verified by building
# and looking inside, because getting this wrong fails silently: the build
# succeeds and simply ships the junk.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.venv/
